{{- /*
  support/channel-post-phase — inline the per-channel `post-<phase>` instruction
  file AT RENDER TIME, as a trailing `##` section.

  These files live at `.mitto/support/<channel-id>/post-<phase>.md` and hold extra
  channel-specific steps to run AFTER the prompt's main work is done (e.g. after an
  investigation has been recorded, or after a reply has been posted).

  Unlike `support/shared/channel-fragment-read`, this fragment:
    - reads with `ReadTemplate` (the file may itself contain `{{ }}` variables),
    - emits a whole `##` section rather than a single bullet,
    - stays SILENT when the channel is known but the file is absent — a missing
      `post-<phase>.md` simply means "nothing extra to do".

  Callers pass named fields via a `dict`:

      Channel:     the Slack channel id (e.g. C0XXXXXXX). Required. Callers that do
                   not know the channel at render time should pass "" — the template
                   then emits a runtime-read instruction as a last-resort fallback.
      Phase:       short stem naming the phase, e.g. "investigate" | "reply". The
                   file read is `post-<Phase>.md`.
      When:        phrase spliced into "apply them **after** <When>", e.g.
                   "the investigation is complete (Steps 5–7)".
      ChannelStep: optional phrase appended after "the bead's `slack_channel` value"
                   in the fallback branch, e.g. " (Step 2)". Omit for none.

  Whitespace contract: the fragment emits its own leading blank line and NO trailing
  newline, and stays completely silent (emits nothing at all) when the channel is
  known but the file is absent. Callers therefore use a LEADING TRIM MARKER so the
  silent case leaves no stray blank line behind:

      {{- template "support/shared/channel-post-phase"
            (dict "Channel" $channel
                  "Phase"   "reply"
                  "When"    "the reply has been posted (Step 7)") }}
*/ -}}
{{- $channel := .Channel -}}
{{- $phase   := .Phase   -}}
{{- $when    := .When    -}}
{{- $path := printf ".mitto/support/%s/post-%s.md" $channel $phase -}}
{{- if and $channel (FileExists $path) }}

## Channel post-{{ $phase }} instructions (embedded from `{{ $path }}`)

These are extra channel-specific instructions for channel `{{ $channel }}`; apply them **after**
{{ $when }}, in addition to everything above.

<!-- BEGIN {{ $path }} -->
{{ ReadTemplate $path . }}
<!-- END {{ $path }} -->
{{- else if eq $channel "" }}

## Channel post-{{ $phase }} instructions (runtime read fallback)

The channel id was not known at render time, so any channel-specific post-{{ $phase }} instructions
could not be inlined. Using the bead's `slack_channel` value{{ if .ChannelStep }}{{ .ChannelStep }}{{ end }}, read
**`.mitto/support/<channel-id>/post-{{ $phase }}.md`**. **If it exists**, apply its instructions
after {{ $when }}. If it does not exist, do nothing extra.
{{- end -}}
{{- /* no trailing newline */ -}}
